Yeah, it is not like Gandalf used a sword or anything.

Nethack is based on D&D.  In original D&D, mages could use daggers
while clerics (priests) could not use edged weapons.

The real problem is spoiled players always going for the same
artifacts.  A better solution might be for the game to pregenerate
which artifacts it will allow in each game at game creation.  It would
pick from the artifact list a pool of available artifacts and if you
wish for one that is not available, you get a message ("That does not
exist").  Of course, the quest artifact would always be generated as
available but everything else would be random.  If a bones file was
loaded with a not allowed artifact, it would be deleted.

 Thus Magicbane might not exist in every game and force spoiled players
to use a different artifact instead.  Using this method, you could
increase the pool of available artifacts without affecting play balance
too much.



